    {
      "kind": "surrounding_passages",
      "title": "From prayer to authorization",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "block_5",
          "text": "The surrounding narrative connects Nehemiah's response to Jerusalem's distress with mourning, fasting, confession, planning, and the request that Artaxerxes authorizes. The rebuilding project therefore follows a movement from remembered covenant crisis to practical imperial permission.",
